'''Michi Fumizuki''' (born 25 March 1987 in [[Santa Creu]], [[Provence]]) is a Baliscan {{W|software engineer}} and [[Confederal Congress|confederal delegate]], currently serving as the incumbent [[Secretariat of Local Administration and Modernization (Balisca)|Secretary of Digitalization]]. Barbieri attended the [[University of Basilisco]], eventually earning a degree in {{W|computer science}}, with a focus in {{W|data science}}. 

Fumizuki's ideology has been self-described as a blend of {{W|social anarchism}} and {{W|pirate politics}}, with an emphasis on {{W|e-democracy}}, {{W|open access}}, and {{W|freedom of expression}}.

Fumizuki is the first openly {{W|transgender}} and {{W|Non-binary gender|non-binary}} confederal secretaries in [[Balisca]]'s history, and they are one of 143 {{W|LGBT demographics|LGBTQ}}-identifying delegates of the current Confederal Congress. 

